# Spreadsheet Close Workflow

You are working with an accountant, not a programmer. Do the matching, sorting and arithmetic yourself and write the result into a working paper. Do not ask the accountant to write code or formulas. Explain what you did in accounting terms.

## Phase order

Do not start a phase until the paper from the phase before it has every `TIE-OUT` row at 0.00.

| Phase | Deliverable | Done when |
|---|---|---|
| 0 Skeleton | `docs/close-plan.md`, one working paper per workpaper in `working/` with headings and empty `TIE-OUT` rows | Every paper opens in Excel or Sheets; the plan states materiality |
| 1 Sources | `working/sources-<period>.csv` | Every file in `data/raw/` listed with row count and control total |
| 2 Reconciliations | `working/recon-<account>-<period>.csv` | Adjusted bank minus adjusted book is 0.00; every unmatched item listed |
| 3 Flux analysis | `working/flux-<period>.csv` | Every account over the threshold has an explanation or `OWNER TO EXPLAIN` |
| 4 JE testing | `working/je-test-<period>.csv` | Every test ran; every exception lists `je_id`, test and source row |
| 5 Close memo | `output/close-memo-<period>.md` | `tie-out-checker` passes; open items have an owner role and a due date |

## Before any analysis

1. Read `docs/close-plan.md` or `plans/interface-contract.md`. It must state the period, the entity, the accounts in scope and materiality. If materiality is missing, stop and ask. Never pick a threshold after seeing results.
2. Copy the source extracts into `data/raw/` once. Then treat them as read-only.
3. Write `working/sources-<period>.csv`: file, rows, control total, what it ties to.

## Where files go

| Kind | Folder | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| Source extracts | `data/raw/` | Read-only. Never edited, sorted, renamed or re-saved |
| Working papers | `working/` | Written by the agent from a template. CSV is the record, XLSX optional |
| Final reports and memo | `output/` | Built from the working papers. Every number traces back |
| Plans, materiality, notes | `docs/`, `plans/` | Written by people and commands |

## Every session ends with

- Every new or changed paper has its `TIE-OUT` rows at 0.00, or the open difference written into the transition doc
- The `tie-out-checker` agent run on anything new in `working/` and `output/`
- No change under `data/raw/`

## In-session commands

| Need | Command |
|---|---|
| Bank or sub-ledger to GL | `/acct-reconcile` |
| Budget vs actual, month over month | `/acct-variance` |
| Journal entry testing | `/acct-je-test` |
| Close memo and handoff | `/acct-close-handoff` |

The `/acct-*` commands were written for both stacks. In this stack:

| Command says | Do this instead |
|---|---|
| write code in `src/` | write the working paper in `working/` from its template |
| write or run `pytest` tie-out tests | fill the paper's `TIE-OUT` rows and confirm each is 0.00 |
| report in `output/` | the working paper goes in `working/`; a short report or the memo goes in `output/` |
| run `tie-out-checker` on `output/` | run it on `working/` and `output/` |
